l back when video_url has no v param'.","The existing fallback tests were written against today's diverged output, so the acceptance tests must add new assertions without editing or weakening any current case.","The ACs do not pin `video_title` (the issue quotes `Test Video` while the test fixture uses `Test Video Title`), so acceptance tests should assert the symptom literals — the `- ` prefix, `(timestamp link unavailable)`, `0:10–0:20`, and `> \"Relevant text\"` — rather than one exact full string.","The `- ` marker must be the first two characters of the returned string on all three fallback paths; a partial fix that adds the marker to only one branch, or that wraps the fallback title in a markdown link (which existing tests forbid), fails.","Red-loop: all three acceptance tests must be RED on the unchanged tree (AC-1/AC-2 fail for want of the snippet blockquote and/or the `- ` marker; AC-3 fails for want of the marker), and at least one red checkpoint's output must contain `> \"Relevant text\"` — the recorded `expected_symptom` — so the deferred repro is provable."],"summary":"Repair the fallback return paths of `formatCitation` in `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts` so an exported citation never loses its transcript snippet or its list formatting: both YouTube fallbacks (`video_url` unparseable, and parseable but with no `v` parameter) must emit the leading `- ` marker and the success-path blockquote line `> \"<snippet>\"`, and the Dynamous fallback with an empty `lesson_url` must gain the `- ` marker while keeping its existing blockquote. The only production file that changes is `exportMarkdown.ts`; acceptance tests are appended to the existing `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts` and every current case must keep passing.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"f4d063ee5a7b4933e7ebd7403a618dea515385a608ec8427a929fb200c81a9c7","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"A